jetsam: turn on the memory-status kill policy the embedded half needs

config/MASTER declares "options CONFIG_JETSAM # <jetsam>", so the option is only
emitted when an activated group lists the token "jetsam". The SWEET MASTER copies
VM_BASE from MASTER.arm64.MacOSX, which does not:

    #  VM_BASE = [ vm_pressure_events memorystatus ... ]

Every embedded MASTER in the tree does list it (MASTER.arm64:65,
MASTER.arm64.iPhoneOS:76, MASTER.arm64.bcm2837:63, MASTER.arm64.BridgeOS:61), and
the official macos profile says the kernel serves the system with the board
embedded memory options, CONFIG_JETSAM included.

Without it the embedded half of vm_compressor.c cannot compile. The extern sits
behind "#if CONFIG_JETSAM" (vm_compressor.c:770-773,
bsd/sys/kern_memorystatus.h:632-636), but two uses at vm_compressor.c:3215 and
:4132 are in the "#else /* XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX */" half with no guard of their own.
With SDKROOT iphoneos, PLATFORM is iPhoneOS, XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX stays undefined,
and the build stops at "use of undeclared identifier memorystatus_swap_all_apps"
(run 42897960519).

--- a/config/MASTER.arm64.sweet
+++ b/config/MASTER.arm64.sweet
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
 #  SCHED_RELEASE =  [ SCHED_BASE ]
 #  SCHED_DEV =      [ SCHED_BASE ]
 #  SCHED_DEBUG =    [ SCHED_BASE config_sched_grrr config_sched_proto ]
-#  VM_BASE =        [ vm_pressure_events memorystatus config_code_decryption encrypted_swap config_deferred_reclaim ]
+#  VM_BASE =        [ vm_pressure_events jetsam memorystatus config_code_decryption encrypted_swap config_deferred_reclaim ]
 #  VM_RELEASE =     [ VM_BASE ]
 #  VM_DEV =         [ VM_BASE dynamic_codesigning pgzalloc ]
 #  VM_DEBUG =       [ VM_BASE dynamic_codesigning pgzalloc ]
